60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"We have three options: A is a flat monthly share, B is a seasonal fixed rate, and C is per-room metering.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option C sounds like a lot of work for the person in charge of the meters! I really don't like the idea of more monthly logging.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option A is simple, but it doesn't address the fact that some of us use far more than others, which might lead to more ""carrying"" rumors.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option C is too expensive to install. Option A still leaves us with volatile monthly payments, which we've seen causes payment delays.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,Option B sounds nice because it's a set figure. It means we don't have to worry about the bill changing every single month.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I strongly favor Option B. It eliminates the ""switch-flicking anxiety"" and creates a stable environment for everyone, regardless of their room's sunlight.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, if we go with B, can we promise to make the year-end settle as simple as possible? I'm voting for B because it's less monthly stress.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Option B provides a compromise. It offers the stability of a fixed cost while ensuring that, eventually, the actual usage is accounted for. I vote B.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,Option B is the most rational choice. It smooths the financial peaks that cause stress and avoids the high installation costs of Option C. I vote B.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,I like Option B too! It sounds the most peaceful and fair for everyone. I vote B!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we are in complete agreement. The psychological benefit of a fixed rate outweighs the minor inconvenience of a yearly adjustment.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm glad we all agree! Let's just make sure we use a simple way to track the total so the end-of-year part isn't too scary!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,A unanimous decision is the best possible outcome for the harmony of this house.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I am satisfied. This approach addresses the volatility of the bills without requiring a significant upfront investment.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'm so happy we could decide this together without any fighting!,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote B.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,I vote B.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I vote B.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
